# Multi-Region Ocean Data Comparison Tool — Implementation Plan

Build a polished, glassmorphism-styled overlay that allows side-by-side comparison of live Argo telemetry across multiple ocean regions. All data flows through the existing Node/Express backend endpoints (`/api/fleet`, `/api/argo/depth-slice`, `/api/validation`).

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Zustand Comparison Store Slice

#### [NEW] [useComparisonStore.js](file:///c:/Users/siddh/Desktop/SIHProject/frontend/3d%20pages/useComparisonStore.js)

A **standalone Zustand store** (not merged into the 1,700-line `useOceanStore.js`) to keep comparison state isolated and avoid conflicts.

**State shape:**
```js
{
  isComparisonOpen: false,       // toggle overlay
  isSearchOpen: false,           // inline search bar visible
  regions: [],                   // array of { id, name, bbox: {lat_min, lat_max, lon_min, lon_max} }
  activeRegionId: null,          // currently selected tab
  regionData: {                  // keyed by region id
    [id]: {
      depth: 0,                  // slider position
      fleet: [],                 // from /api/fleet
      selectedFloat: null,       // chosen platform from fleet
      depthSlice: null,          // from /api/argo/depth-slice
      validation: null,          // from /api/validation
      isLoadingFleet: false,
      isLoadingSlice: false,
      isLoadingValidation: false,
    }
  }
}
```

**Actions:**
- `openComparison()` / `closeComparison()`
- `toggleSearch()`
- `addRegion(name)` — maps name → bounding box using a dictionary, adds to `regions[]`, auto-opens overlay
- `removeRegion(id)` — removes region tab/panel
- `setRegionDepth(id, depth)` — updates the depth slider for a panel
- `selectFloat(id, platform)` — picks an argo float from the fleet list
- `fetchFleet(id)` — calls `GET /api/fleet?lat_min=&lat_max=&lon_min=&lon_max=`
- `fetchDepthSlice(id)` — calls `GET /api/argo/depth-slice?platform_number=${selectedFloat}&depth=${depth}`
- `fetchValidation(id)` — calls `GET /api/validation?platform_number=${selectedFloat}&depth=${depth}`

**Region bounding box dictionary** (built-in, extensible):

| Region | lat_min | lat_max | lon_min | lon_max |
|--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|
| Arabian Sea | 5 | 25 | 55 | 78 |
| Bay of Bengal | 5 | 22 | 78 | 98 |
| Lakshadweep Sea | 8 | 14 | 70 | 77 |
| Andaman Sea | 5 | 18 | 92 | 100 |
| Indian Ocean | 0 | 25 | 55 | 98 |
| South China Sea | 0 | 23 | 100 | 121 |
| Red Sea | 12 | 30 | 32 | 44 |
| Persian Gulf | 24 | 30 | 48 | 56 |

